Every Subject is checked against its Schema as you edit it. Each constraint carries a severity: warnings inform, errors block saving on wikis that enforce validation. This wiki does not, so invalid values are stored, and the editor shows their violations again when reopened.

== Try it ==

Open the Data tab of [[Validation Clean]], choose '''Edit''', and break a value: clear the Title, set the Score to 150, or change a Tags entry to <code>ftp://example.com</code>. Each violation appears at its field with its severity.

{| class="wikitable"
! Property !! Constraint !! Severity
|-
| Title || required || error
|-
| Summary || 10 to 100 characters || warning
|-
| Aliases || no duplicate entries || warning
|-
| Homepage || required, a valid URL || error
|-
| Tags || valid URLs || error, fixed
|-
| Score || 0 to 100 || error
|-
| Status || required, one of three options || warning
|-
| Release date || 2020 to 2030 || warning
|-
| Last reviewed || 2020 to 2030, with time || warning
|-
| Related product || must point at a Product || error, fixed
|}

== How this is built ==

* [[Schema:Validation Demo]]; the Schema editor sets the severity per constraint.
* [https://neowiki.ai/docs/api/schema-format#constraint-severity Constraint severity] and [https://neowiki.ai/docs/api/validation-codes Validation codes] in the documentation.
* [{{SERVER}}{{SCRIPTPATH}}/rest.php/neowiki/v0/schema/Validation_Demo/json-schema This Schema as a JSON Schema document], stating every constraint whatever its severity; [https://neowiki.ai/docs/api/json-schema JSON Schema] in the documentation.
